1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,540
Let me give you a live example from my career.

2
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:06,945
I had to launch a consumer to enterprise product,

3
00:00:06,945 --> 00:00:11,295
which means I had to convert users from consumers to paying customers.

4
00:00:11,295 --> 00:00:13,920
Not an easy task by any means because

5
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:16,860
nobody really wants to pay when they can get it for free.

6
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:21,570
In order to convince our potential customers that product worth paying for,

7
00:00:21,570 --> 00:00:24,780
I had to work very close with my marketing partner.

8
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:29,445
In fact, she was basically part of our team for the whole process.

9
00:00:29,445 --> 00:00:33,135
We saw product success as a shared responsibility.

10
00:00:33,135 --> 00:00:35,975
First, we worked together to

11
00:00:35,975 --> 00:00:39,555
outline the advantage of our product versus the free version.

12
00:00:39,555 --> 00:00:41,375
Once we have that,

13
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:46,850
my product marketing manager went ahead and created a landing page for our product.

14
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:49,860
She incorporated all the elements we discussed.

15
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:51,230
Once that was done,

16
00:00:51,230 --> 00:00:55,325
we reviewed it as a team and agreed on testing to pick the winning version.

17
00:00:55,325 --> 00:00:57,590
In parallel, we had to work on

18
00:00:57,590 --> 00:01:01,540
different promotions to actually bring our users to the landing page.

19
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:05,000
Once again, my marketing partner was there to help.

20
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,210
She crafted multiple messages to our users

21
00:01:08,210 --> 00:01:12,845
and I supported her by creating multiple tests to validate our best promotion.

22
00:01:12,845 --> 00:01:15,015
In order to prepare for the launch,

23
00:01:15,015 --> 00:01:17,450
she also worked with different marketing team across

24
00:01:17,450 --> 00:01:20,510
the globe to get local support in different countries.

25
00:01:20,510 --> 00:01:23,600
Not to mention that all this marketing partners checked

26
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:26,795
out translation a couple more times just to be sure.

27
00:01:26,795 --> 00:01:29,625
Once we launched, we didn't stop partnering,

28
00:01:29,625 --> 00:01:32,450
we actually develop a mutual road map which involved

29
00:01:32,450 --> 00:01:35,090
product features supported by marketing campaigns.

30
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:38,795
It was important to show a united front, our leadership,

31
00:01:38,795 --> 00:01:43,420
so that we have the support of both product and marketing for future development.

32
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:46,610
One of my favorite parts of that project was actually having

33
00:01:46,610 --> 00:01:51,670
a great sounding board who thinks about the product strategy and user needs with me.

34
00:01:51,670 --> 00:01:53,690
In my role today,

35
00:01:53,690 --> 00:01:55,880
I always have recurring meetings with

36
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:59,360
my partners to make sure they're not missing anything.

37
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:02,720
That way, I'm involved in what our partner teams are

38
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:08,610
thinking and they know all the new items coming out of our product team.

